{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/383282-idigam-the-silicon-empress","id":383282,"title":"Idigam: The Silicon Empress","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-27T10:35:09-08:00","id":383282,"title":"Idigam: The Silicon Empress","content":"I came up with this many years ago for my first WtF campaign and was pretty proud of it. <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><b>Silicon Empress</b> is merely her title as the leader of the Silicon Court (which consisted of spirits of the Internet). Her actual name is </span></span><i>Kinugal</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">, First Tongue for &quot;Place That Isn't&quot;. She was a part of the campaign for over a year before they figured out she was an idigam and not just a powerful Incarna.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Legend</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Kinugal was a powerful spirit of places which don't exist. She effectively straddled the Border Marches and pulled humans into herself whenever they imagined places that did not exist, changing herself to match their phantom realm and harvesting the Essence she was able to generate until finally devouring their souls. Father Wolf had a difficult time fighting her, since she was almost a state of mind rather than a place or a person. In time, however, his pack found her in their dreams and he bound her, saying, &quot;Place That Isn't, you are bound from the world until such time as I return.&quot; Then they left, intending never to return. For untold years, she was locked out of the world, only able to touch it briefly through the dreams and imaginings of humanity, over which she still had sway, but these contacts were too brief and she was only able to glean enough Essence to survive.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Modern History</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Then, one day, she sensed an imaginary place that lasted longer than the span of a night's sleep or the time it took to read a good book. She touches this new place and its spirit, woke it, and influenced it as it grew. This spirit was the Internet. With its arrival, she found a whole new world to influence, one very close to the Material and Spiritual worlds which she was bound from. Only able to influence, never able to cross over, she insinuated herself among the Information spirits who lived there and set herself as their brood lord. They gather Essence for her, opening windows into the material world and drawing it from those who use computers, phones, or any device which contacts telecommunication networks, using their Influence to invoke more extreme emotional states to generate even more Essence.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Release</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Kinugal seeks a piece of Father Wolf so that she can break the binding preventing her from entering the world. She is looking to manipulate the pack into getting it for her through bribes of services and, eventually, threats and demands for recompense. Once they have it, she will have the Internet act as the bridge to bring it through the Spirit World to her and she will be free, at which time she will consume the Internet and begin molding it to her needs.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Storytelling Hints</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">While she seems comprehensible for an idigam, Kinugal is still a very alien creature, she just happens to have a fairly simple goal in mind at present. Should she be released of her bindings, she would began to remake the Internet into the shifting, unreal realm she used to represent and start pulling humans into it in order to feed from them, changing the landscape to draw the most Essence from them. She will also try and reshape the real world. Her main weakness is that she doesn't have any concept of what is or isn't &quot;real&quot;. Her realm is a mutable one of endless possibilities, so she has no grasp that some things aren't possible in the real world.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Bane</b></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Her bane is something dead from the real world. My PCs fulfilled this by hijacking a bone of Father Wolf from a group of Pure cultists. This also, inadvertently, freed her from her bindings (since Father Wolf had returned). It made for an outstanding encounter as they rushed to use it to bind her while she exerted her full power.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}